Hello,

I am a relative novice, so I apologize if I use the wrong terminology or the issue is very obvious.  But the problem I'm having is that when I run a MplusAutomator command line in R (e.g., createModels("~/Documents/template.inp"), it is "registered" but never produces output or an error message of any sort and I have to restart the program.

I am using Rstudio 4.0.3 on a Mac, I re-installed MplusAutomation from CRAN, and I updated Xcode beta.  Prior to updating Xcode, I was receiving an error message: missing xcrun at: /library/developer/commandlinetools/usr/bin/xcrun.  Installing the new Xcode seemed to resolve this error, but as I said, now there is not output at all.

Thank you for any suggestions about how to problem solve this issue!
Whitney

